    {
     "tagName": "v0.1.0",
     "publishedAt": "2026-10-14T17:16:37Z",
     "description": "**Your GitHub profile and repositories, at a glance.** glancecard renders SVG cards for your READMEs and commits them from a GitHub Action in your own repository: no server, no third-party service, no dependencies.\r\n\r\n<picture>\r\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gfazioli/glancecard/v0.1.0/docs/examples/octoscope-dark.svg\">\r\n  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gfazioli/glancecard/v0.1.0/docs/examples/octoscope-light.svg\" width=\"880\" alt=\"A repository card for gfazioli/octoscope\">\r\n</picture>\r\n\r\n### Cards\r\n- **Repository card**: status, age and latest tag, description and topics, commits in the last 30 days with a 26-week sparkline, twelve stat tiles, a year of commits with streaks, the weekly rhythm (day × hour), languages and essentials, the latest commits and releases with their cadence, contributors. Sections can be left out.\r\n- **Profile card**: followers, stars, repositories, pull requests, issues, commits, the contribution calendar, the most starred repositories and their languages.\r\n- **Dark and light**: one file each, for a `<picture>` that follows the reader's GitHub theme.\r\n\r\n### Use it\r\n```yaml\r\n- uses: actions/checkout@v7\r\n- uses: gfazioli/glancecard@v0.1.0\r\n  with:\r\n    profile: your-login\r\n    repos: your-login/your-repo\r\n```\r\nPreview from a terminal: `npx github:gfazioli/glancecard repo owner/name`. Inputs, the `<picture>` snippet and the FAQ are in the [README](https://github.com/gfazioli/glancecard#readme).\r\n\r\n### Safe by default\r\n- Private repositories are refused unless `allow-private: true`: their card would publish their data.\r\n- A history longer than `max-commits` is stated on the card instead of undercounted.\r\n- Every request has a deadline: a stalled host fails one card instead of hanging the job.\r\n- On a pull request the cards are rendered, never committed.\r\n"
    }
   ]
  },
